[h1]Cosmic War[/h1]
[i]The definitive diplomatic warfare, mercenary, and conquest expansion for the Cosmic Series.[/i]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]What is Cosmic War?[/h2]
Bring total war to the galaxy! [b]Cosmic War[/b] transforms static NPC empires into aggressive, expanding juggernauts. Watch as factions build up War Heat, declare devastating wars, lay siege to fortified sectors, and offer you lucrative contracts to shift the balance of power. Every action you take has diplomatic consequences — and now, every war has a real scoreboard, a real location on the map, and a real cost for losing.

[b]⚠️ REQUIRED DEPENDENCY:[/b] Cosmic War is part of the "Core 5" Cosmic Series mods which are hard dependencies for each other. You [b]must[/b] be subscribed to all [b]REQUIRED ITEMS[/b] to play!

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Core Features[/h2]
[list]
[*]🔥 [b]Dynamic War Heat & Subspace Tears:[/b] Watch tensions rise. At critical levels, factions detonate experimental Subspace Weapons, tearing the fabric of space and unleashing localized Rifts!
[*]🛡️ [b]Frontline Sieges & Dreadnoughts:[/b] Factions dynamically siege enemy territory, spearheaded by massive Siege Dreadnoughts with 5x shield multipliers. A siege launched far from home also drags along a supply convoy — destroy it to collapse the whole siege.
[*]🗺️ [b]Frontlines:[/b] The galaxy map now shows exactly where two warring factions' territory touches, live. Fight there for denser patrols, more War Events, and better contract pay.
[*]⚔️ [b]War Score & Attrition:[/b] Every war tracks a real scoreboard of kills and territory. A faction that's genuinely losing shows it — smaller patrols, worse station prices, a real push toward peace — and a lopsided enough war ends outright in a Decisive Victory.
[*]🏚️ [b]Occupation & Insurgency:[/b] A freshly conquered sector isn't fully settled — for a while after, the old owner's loyalists may raid the new occupiers.
[*]🕵️ [b]Intelligence Network:[/b] Recon and sabotage contracts bank Intel against the faction you're scouting — spend it to preview an expanding rival's next move, or to unlock a Defector Debrief.
[*]🤝 [b]Humanitarian Contracts:[/b] Not every job is a fight. Deliver relief supplies to a starving faction, broker aid or sanctions relief at a Trading Post, or break a blockade choking a patron's supply lines.
[*]🌑 [b]Coalition Ceasefires:[/b] When the Eclipse becomes a serious galaxy-wide threat, every warring faction is pulled into a temporary truce. Old grudges wait when something worse is coming for everyone.
[*]⚡ [b]Electronic Warfare & Weather Sieges:[/b] Sieges carry up to a 35% chance to EMP burst ALL shields to 0 (15% in open fleet clashes). Sieges under Dark Matter Fog slice defender boarding resistance in half!
[*]🏰 [b]Planetary Defense Grids:[/b] Threatened factions can commission a Planetary Shield Generator at their home sector, rendering every station in the sector invincible until it's destroyed.
[*]🌍 [b]Dynamic Territory Expansion:[/b] Factions physically conquer stations with AI Troop Transports and permanently expand their borders on the Galaxy Map. A war at maximum intensity can even tear open a permanent subspace corridor between two capitals.
[*]💰 [b]Mercenary Enlistment & Letters of Marque:[/b] Sign a standing commission with a faction at war and their enemies mark you hostile immediately, and their Military Outposts patch up your hull at a privateer's rate — but turn your guns on your patron, and the commission is revoked on the spot.
[*]⚔️ [b]22 Dynamic War Contracts & Events:[/b] Scaling combat missions (Force Recon, Corridor Interdiction, Armistice Escort, Decapitation Strike, and more) and roaming flashpoints — border checkpoints, prisoner convoys, mutinies, blockade runners — as the war unfolds around you.
[*]🏅 [b]Bounty Licenses:[/b] Land the first blow on a faction's active bounty target to open a 45-minute License worth up to 15 kills: stations pay 10x, Dreadnoughts and bosses pay 5x, and everything else still pays its full share.
[*]💵 [b]Warbonds:[/b] Buy war bonds from a Trading Post while a war is raging. Returns scale smoothly with how the war actually goes, or cash out early for a flat 40% if it's turning ugly.
[*]🎭 [b]9 Dynamic Faction Traits:[/b] Factions are generated with traits like 'Entrenched' or 'Imperialist' (The Eclipse is hardcoded both Imperialist AND Vengeful!), altering their AI aggressiveness and mercenary payouts.
[*]🤝 [b]Alliance PvP Mirroring:[/b] Triggering a diplomatic incident spreads consequences permanently to your entire Player Alliance, which now also shares one pooled Intel balance per scouted faction.
[*]📉 [b]Deep Economy Warfare:[/b] Market collapses natively trigger desperation invasions! Factions with severe Famine Scores launch massive assaults on wealthy neighbors to survive — or accept a delivery of relief supplies instead.
[*]📊 [b]Galactic Politics Tab, Rebuilt:[/b] Four real sub-tabs — Conflicts, Dossier, War Room, and Legend. Sort every active war by War Score, pull up a full faction profile in one click, and see your own Bounty License, Warbonds, and Intel in one place.
[*]🩸 [b]Cinematic Battlefield HUD:[/b] Enter a contested sector and watch a live split red/blue bar, with the current War Score, tell you exactly how close that frontline is to flipping.
[*]📈 [b]Persistent Diplomacy Drift & Sanctions:[/b] Political relationships evolve in the background. Deep rivalries trigger trade sanctions.
[*]🕊️ [b]Ceasefire & Détente:[/b] Conflict cycles de-escalate as factions exhaust resources and grow weary of losing, resulting in fragile peace periods. Vengeful factions will NEVER accept ceasefires!
[*]📰 [b]Galactic News Network:[/b] War bulletins, humanitarian deliveries, captured ships, and toppled home sectors all make the news — the biggest moments flagged as Breaking.
[*]⚙️ [b]Cross-Mod Synergy:[/b] War Profiteering pushes Cosmic Overhaul station trade income up to 300% higher at max War Heat. A resolved siege has a 1-in-20 chance to leave behind a Cosmic Chronicles Propaganda Beacon for scavengers to find.
[/list]

